# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "instantiatesClass" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een SKOS-conceptschema aan de ontologieklasse die zijn concepten specialiseren: een concept uit dit schema wordt gebruikt als het rdf:type van een instantie van die klasse."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a SKOS concept scheme to the ontology class its concepts specialise: a concept from this scheme is used as the rdf:type of an instance of that class."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "instantiates class"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "instantieert klasse"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#instantiatesClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme> .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "nodeKind" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Classificeert hoe instanties van een klasse in de gegenereerde graaf worden gerealiseerd: mda:Individuated, mda:Referential of mda:Stateful."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Classifies how instances of a class are realised in the generated graph: mda:Individuated, mda:Referential, or mda:Stateful."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "knooppuntsoort"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "node kind"@en .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "persistsPostAlarm" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Markeert een objecteigenschap waarvan de afgeleide feiten over een technisch knooppunt blijven bestaan gedurende het PostAlarmValidScheme-venster nadat het alarm dat ze afleidde is beëindigd."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Marks an object property whose entailed facts about a technical node persist for the PostAlarmValidScheme window after the alarm that entailed them ends, the same way mda:hasOperationState already did — see 4_OPERATIONAL/op_knowledge.py's inferred_states."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "blijft bestaan na alarm"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "persists post alarm"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#persistsPostAlarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "postAlarmValidityDuration" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Duration after alarm end for which assertions from this scheme remain valid. Absence of this annotation on a scheme implies alarm-duration only (PT0S)."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Duur na het alarm-einde gedurende welke beweringen geldig blijven. Afwezigheid impliceert alleen geldig tijdens alarm (PT0S)."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "post-alarm geldigheidsduur"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "post-alarm validity duration"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#postAlarmValidityDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#duration> .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "refinesParticularIdentity" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Markeert een blad-eigenschap waarvan de waarde één gemunt deeltje onderscheidt van een ander van hetzelfde type onder dezelfde eigenaar in de werkelijke wereld — verwerkt in de IRI van het deeltje bij grondingstijd, niet in een vocabulaireconcept."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Marks a leaf property whose value distinguishes one minted particular from another of the same type under the same real-world owner — folded into the particular's IRI at grounding time, not into a vocabulary concept."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "refines particular identity"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "verfijnt particuliere identiteit"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "refinesUniversalIdentity" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Markeert een blad-eigenschap waarvan de waarde voorcoördineert tot een gedeeld universeel concept op vocabulaireniveau, in plaats van de per-alarm/per-eigenaar toestand te beschrijven. De waarde benoemt een soort, herbruikbaar over eigenaren heen — geen plaatsing."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Marks a leaf property whose value pre-coordinates into a shared universal concept at the vocabulary layer, rather than describing per-alarm/per-owner state. The value names a kind, reusable across owners — not a placement."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "refines universal identity"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "verfijnt universele identiteit"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "situational" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Markeert een objecteigenschap waarvan de afgeleide beweringen behoren tot een situationele export per alarm, in tegenstelling tot achtergrond-/taxonomische structuur die een reasoner raadpleegt maar die zelf nooit wordt geëxporteerd."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Marks an object property whose entailed assertions belong in a per-alarm situational export, as opposed to background/taxonomic structure (e.g. rdfs:subClassOf) that a reasoner consults but that is never itself exported."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "situational"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "situationeel"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "valuesFromScheme" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een objecteigenschap aan het SKOS-conceptschema waaruit zijn waarden afkomstig zijn."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links an object property to the SKOS concept scheme from which its values are drawn."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "values from scheme"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "waarden uit schema"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme> .
