# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#TherapeuticModality> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "administers" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een apparaat aan de therapeutische modaliteit die het toedient."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a device to the therapeutic modality it administers."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "administers"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#administers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "toegediend"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Signal> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#SignalAnalysis> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "analyzedBy" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een signaal aan de signaalanalysestap die het verbruikt. De enige weg naar mda:SignalAnalysis — bewust niet ook rechtstreeks bereikbaar vanaf mda:FunctionalUnit (er bestaat geen performsAnalysis-achtige kortere weg), zodat er precies één pad naar een analysestap bestaat, altijd via het specifieke signaal (de specifieke signalen) dat het daadwerkelijk verbruikt. Functioneel niet: hetzelfde signaal kan meer dan één analysestap voeden."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a signal to the signal-analysis step that consumes it. The only edge reaching mda:SignalAnalysis — deliberately not also reachable directly from mda:FunctionalUnit (no performsAnalysis-style shortcut exists), so there is exactly one path to an analysis step, always through the specific signal(s) it actually consumes. A second, shorter path would let ontology_tree.py's shortest-path class-tree derivation silently prefer it over the precise one (the same failure mode mda:administers was introduced to avoid for mda:TherapeuticModality — see the Technical axioms note in inference.ttl). Not functional: the same signal can feed more than one analysis step (e.g. ECG lead II feeds both a heart-rate computation and an aVF derivation)."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "analyzed by"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#analyzedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "geanalyseerd door"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Metric> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#PhysiologicalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "approximates" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een metriek aan de fysiologische eigenschap die het benadert."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a metric to the physiological property it approximates."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "approximates"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#approximates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "benadert"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Patient> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "concernsPatient" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een alarmbericht aan de patiënt die het betreft — het gedeelde, persistente samenvoegankerpunt. Bewust een doodlopend pad: leidt niet langer via mda:isMonitoredBy naar mda:Device. Functioneel: één bericht betreft precies één patiënt."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an alarm message to the patient it concerns — the shared, persistent merge anchor. Deliberately a dead end: it no longer continues on to mda:Device via mda:isMonitoredBy (see mda:triggeredBy's comment for why). Functional: one message concerns exactly one patient — it is minted fresh per alarm precisely so it never needs to concern more than one."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "betreft patiënt"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#concernsPatient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concerns patient"@en .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Sensor> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasAnatomicalPosition" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een sensor aan zijn anatomische positie op het lichaam. Functioneel: een fysieke sensor bevindt zich op een gegeven moment op precies één positie."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a sensor to its anatomical position on the body. Functional: a physical sensor occupies exactly one position at a time."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has anatomical position"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasAnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft anatomische positie"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge/vocab/alarm-category/Scheme> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasCategory" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De categorie van het alarm (beschrijvend, naast label en prioriteit)."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The category of the alarm (a descriptive, alongside label and priority)."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has category"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft categorie"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#InverseFunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasComponent" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een apparaat aan zijn onderdelen, al dan niet sensorisch (bijv. een aansluitpoort, voedingseenheid, verwarmingselement of functionele eenheid). Invers-functioneel: een onderdeel behoort tot hoogstens één apparaat — er is geen aparte isComponentOf-eigenschap; bevraag alleen in deze richting."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a device to its components, sensing or not (e.g. a connection port, power unit, heating element, or functional unit). Inverse-functional: a component belongs to at most one device — no separate isComponentOf property is declared; query in this direction only."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has component"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft onderdeel"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasOperationState> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge/vocab/operation-state/Scheme> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasComponentOperationState" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De operationele status van een niet-sensorisch onderdeel, bijv. Disconnected of Warning. Een subeigenschap van hasOperationState met een enkel benoemd domein, zodat CSV-gestuurde readout het ondubbelzinnig kan koppelen."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The operational state of a non-sensing component, e.g. Disconnected or Warning. A sub-property of hasOperationState with a single named domain, so CSV-driven readout can attach it unambiguously."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has component operation state"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponentOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft onderdeeloperatiestatus"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasOperationState> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge/vocab/operation-state/Scheme> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasDeviceOperationState" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De operationele status van een apparaat zelf, bijv. Disconnected. Een subeigenschap van hasOperationState met een enkel benoemd domein, zodat CSV-gestuurde readout het ondubbelzinnig kan koppelen."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The operational state of a device itself, e.g. Disconnected. A sub-property of hasOperationState with a single named domain, so CSV-driven readout can attach it unambiguously."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has device operation state"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft apparaatoperatiestatus"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge/vocab/device-type/Scheme> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasDeviceType" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Het specifieke type of de modelaanduiding van het apparaat (bijv. ServoU)."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The specific type or model designation of the device (e.g. ServoU)."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has device type"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasDeviceType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft apparaattype"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasComponent> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#InverseFunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasFunctionalUnit" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een apparaat aan een functionele eenheid die het bevat (bijv. een ECG-module, een SpO2-module) — een subeigenschap van hasComponent, aangezien elke functionele eenheid een onderdeel is. Invers-functioneel: een functionele eenheid behoort tot hoogstens één apparaat."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a device to a functional unit it houses (e.g. an ECG module, an SpO2 module) — a sub-property of hasComponent, since every functional unit is a component. Inverse-functional: a functional unit belongs to at most one device."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has functional unit"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft functionele eenheid"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge/vocab/alarm-label/Scheme> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasLabelConcept" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een alarmtype aan zijn gecontroleerde-vocabulaireconcept in het schema van mda:AlarmLabel — één concept per onderscheidend labelstring, gedeeld door elk archetype dat dat label gebruikt, ongeacht prioriteit."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an alarm type to its controlled-vocabulary concept in mda:AlarmLabel's scheme — one concept per distinct label string encountered, shared across every archetype that uses that label regardless of priority (2_READOUT/vocab_readout.py's label_concept_iri keys on the label alone, not the archetype). The companion of mda:hasLabel, not a replacement for it."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has label concept"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabelConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft labelconcept"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Sensor> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesParticularIdentity> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasLaterality" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een sensor aan zijn lateraliteit (links, rechts, bilateraal). Functioneel: een fysieke sensor heeft op een gegeven moment precies één lateraliteit."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a sensor to its laterality (left, right, bilateral). Functional: a physical sensor has exactly one laterality at a time."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has laterality"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLaterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft lateraliteit"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#refinesUniversalIdentity> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge/vocab/manufacturer/Scheme> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasManufacturer" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De fabrikant of productlijn van het apparaat."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The manufacturer or product line of the device."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has manufacturer"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasManufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft fabrikant"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#InverseFunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasMessage" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Het bericht van het alarm: een per-alarm mda:AlarmMessage-knooppunt met de onafhankelijke facetten van de gebeurtenis — mda:concernsPatient en mda:triggeredBy — als nevengeschikte eigenschappen, geen van beide via de ander bereikt. Functioneel en invers-functioneel: één alarm heeft precies één bericht en één bericht hoort bij precies één alarm."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The alarm's message: a per-alarm mda:AlarmMessage node carrying the occurrence's independent facets — mda:concernsPatient (who this alarm is about) and mda:triggeredBy (what caused it) — as siblings, neither reached through the other (see mda:triggeredBy's comment for why they used to be chained and no longer are). Distinct per alarm so many alarms can reference the same shared patient/device and merge there. Functional and inverse-functional: one alarm has exactly one message and one message belongs to exactly one alarm — alarm_iri/message_iri are minted from the same (device_id, start) key in 4_OPERATIONAL/op_knowledge.py precisely to keep this a bijection."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has message"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft bericht"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasOperationState
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
