# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Sensor> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasSensor" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een functionele eenheid aan de fysieke sensor(en) waarvan het afleest (bijv. een ECG-module aan elk van zijn 12 afleidingen). GEEN subeigenschap van hasComponent: het domein is FunctionalUnit, niet Device, en het domein van hasComponent ligt vast op Device. Een sensor behoort niet langer rechtstreeks tot een apparaat."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a functional unit to the physical sensor(s) it reads from (e.g. an ECG module to each of its 12 leads). NOT a sub-property of hasComponent: its domain is FunctionalUnit, not Device, and hasComponent's domain is fixed to Device — declaring it a sub-property would wrongly entail every FunctionalUnit is itself a Device. A sensor no longer belongs directly to a device (see FunctionalUnit below for why: the sensor is the physical probe, the functional unit is what analyses what it picks up). Deliberately NOT owl:InverseFunctionalProperty, unlike most of this file's other IFP-marked relations: 2_READOUT/outcome/inference.ttl's FunctionalUnit recipe axioms assert hasSensor via an owl:hasValue restriction, so every alarm typed to the same FunctionalUnit concept (e.g. every FU_PneumoTachograph alarm) entails hasSensor to the SAME shared sensor concept, not a fresh individual per alarm the way 2_READOUT/vocab_readout.py's own per-row blank nodes do. Confirmed by an isolated reasoner test: with InverseFunctionalProperty declared, prp-ifp forces every one of those alarms' FunctionalUnit individuals into owl:sameAs with each other — and would do the same across grounded, per-patient data in 4_OPERATIONAL if this property were ever reasoned over there, merging different patients' equipment. mda:producesSignal carries the same latent risk if a future recipe axiom (e.g. the pending ECG one) ever reuses one signal concept across two different sensor concepts — watch for it there too."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has sensor"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft sensor"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasOperationState> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Sensor> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#valuesFromScheme> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge/vocab/operation-state/Scheme> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasSensorOperationState" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De operationele status van een sensor, bijv. Enabled, Disabled of Malfunction. Een subeigenschap van hasOperationState met een enkel benoemd domein, zodat CSV-gestuurde readout het ondubbelzinnig kan koppelen."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The operational state of a sensor, e.g. Enabled, Disabled, or Malfunction. A sub-property of hasOperationState with a single named domain, so CSV-driven readout can attach it unambiguously."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has sensor operation state"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasSensorOperationState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft sensoroperatiestatus"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#InverseFunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Patient> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "isMonitoredBy" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een patiënt aan het apparaat dat hen op dit moment bewaakt. Invers-functioneel: een apparaat bewaakt hoogstens één patiënt tegelijk."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a patient to the device currently monitoring them. No longer part of the blueprint's structural path to mda:Device (see mda:triggeredBy) — that routing asserted every alarm-raising device 'monitors' the patient, which overclaims for a therapeutic one. What remains is this property's own, separate justification: inverse-functional, a device monitors at most one patient at a time — a physical monitor is not shared between two patients simultaneously, even though it may serve different patients at different times — so a reasoner can catch a double-booking directly (as an entailed owl:sameAs between two asserted-distinct patients) rather than relying on generator discipline, the same pattern as mda:hasSensor/mda:producesSignal below. Only meaningful if isMonitoredBy is asserted per-instant, not as a standing fact for a patient's whole encounter — see 4_OPERATIONAL/op_knowledge.py, the only place it is still asserted."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is monitored by"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isMonitoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "wordt bewaakt door"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "isOfType" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een concrete alarminstantie aan zijn archetypische alarmtype in de typecatalogus, waaruit standaard structurele kennis (apparaattype, sensortype, signaaltype) kan worden geërfd. Functioneel: één alarminstantie is van precies één archetype."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a concrete alarm instance to its archetypal alarm type in the type catalogue, from which default structural knowledge (device type, sensor type, signal type) can be inherited. Functional: one alarm occurrence is of exactly one archetype."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is of type"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#isOfType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is van type"@nl .
