# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#InverseFunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:genid16 .
_:genid16 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:genid18 .
_:genid18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid17 .
_:genid17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:genid17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#SignalAnalysis> .
_:genid17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Sensor> .
_:genid18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid16 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Signal> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "producesSignal" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een sensor OF een signaalanalysestap aan het signaal dat het produceert — het ruwe signaal van een sensor, of het afgeleide/tussenliggende signaal van een analysestap (bijv. versterkte afleiding aVF, gecombineerd uit andere afleidingen). Invers-functioneel: een signaal heeft hoogstens één producent, ongeacht het soort."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a sensor OR a signal-analysis step to the signal it produces — a sensor's raw signal, or an analysis step's derived/intermediate signal (e.g. augmented lead aVF, combined from other leads). Inverse-functional: a signal has at most one producer, whichever kind produced it. Its domain is a union, so it cannot itself anchor 2_READOUT/vocab_readout.py's CSV/tree derivation (ontology_tree.py's derive_class_tree only follows a named rdfs:domain, the same limitation documented at mda:hasOperationState below) — mda:sensorProducesSignal is the single-domain sub-property that does. A signal-analysis step's own derived-signal output (the aVF case) is only ever hand-authored in inference.ttl, never CSV-driven, so it uses this general property directly and needs no sub-property of its own."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "produceert signaal"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "produces signal"@en .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#producesSignal> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Sensor> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Signal> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "sensorProducesSignal" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Het CSV/boom-gerichte geval van mda:producesSignal: het eigen ruwe signaal van een sensor. Een subeigenschap met één domein, zodat de door 2_READOUT/vocab_readout.py afgeleide boom Signal ondubbelzinnig onder Sensor kan hangen."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The CSV/tree-facing case of mda:producesSignal: a sensor's own raw signal. A single-domain sub-property so 2_READOUT/vocab_readout.py's ontology-derived tree can attach Signal under Sensor unambiguously — see mda:producesSignal's comment. Every fact asserted through it still entails the general mda:producesSignal fact (and, transitively, mda:hasOperationState's propagation chain) via rdfs:subPropertyOf."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sensor produceert signaal"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#sensorProducesSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sensor produces signal"@en .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#TherapeuticModality> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#PhysiologicalProcess> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#situational> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "targetsProcess" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een therapeutische modaliteit aan het fysiologische proces waarop het zich richt."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a therapeutic modality to the physiological process it targets."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "richt zich op proces"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#targetsProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "targets process"@en .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "triggeredBy" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Koppelt een alarmbericht rechtstreeks aan het apparaat waarvan het de technische structuur impliceert — de enige weg van AlarmMessage naar de mda:Device-deelboom. Vervangt routering via mda:concernsPatient/mda:isMonitoredBy: die keten beweerde dat elk alarmerend apparaat de patiënt 'bewaakt', wat onjuist is voor een wezenlijk therapeutisch apparaat. mda:isMonitoredBy zelf is ONGEWIJZIGD en blijft gebruikt, maar uitsluitend voor de eigen operationele rechtvaardiging. Functioneel, niet invers-functioneel."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an alarm message directly to the device whose technical structure it implicates — the sole path from AlarmMessage into the mda:Device subtree (mda:hasFunctionalUnit, mda:hasSensor, ...). Replaces routing that reach through mda:concernsPatient/mda:isMonitoredBy: that chain asserted every alarm-raising device 'monitors' the patient, which is false for a fundamentally therapeutic device (mda:MechanicalVentilator, mda:Dialysator, mda:ExtracorporealMembraneOxygenator, mda:Incubator/mda:Thermoregulator all administer a therapy — see mda:administers — rather than principally observe). mda:isMonitoredBy itself is UNCHANGED and still used, but only for its own actual justification: 4_OPERATIONAL/op_knowledge.py's per-instant double-booking check, asserted fresh at grounding time, never derived from or dependent on this blueprint-level structure. Functional, not inverse-functional: one message has exactly one triggering device, but one device triggers many messages over its lifetime — unlike mda:hasMessage's strict bijection."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "triggered by"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "veroorzaakt door"@nl .
