# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "hasLabel" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Het vrije-tekstlabel dat een alarmtype identificeert, exact zoals het in de brondata voorkomt — een literal, geen concept. mda:hasLabelConcept is de bijbehorende gecontroleerde-vocabulaire lezing van hetzelfde label; beide worden bewust bijgehouden. AlarmType is het enige domein; een Alarm-instantie bereikt zijn label via mda:isOfType."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The free-text label identifying an alarm type, exactly as it occurs in the source data (e.g. 'PHILIPSMONITOR - SpO2 geen pols') — a literal, not a concept: alarm labels routinely contain spaces and punctuation no SKOS notation can carry. mda:hasLabelConcept is the companion controlled-vocabulary reading of the same label — the two are deliberately BOTH kept, not alternatives: this ontology wants both the label as encountered and a stable, deduplicated vocabulary entry for it (the same label recurs across archetypes that differ only in priority). AlarmType is its only domain; a plain Alarm instance reaches its label via mda:isOfType."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has label"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#hasLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heeft label"@nl .
# 
