# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "Alarm" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A notification or alert generated by a medical device."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Een melding of waarschuwing gegenereerd door een medisch apparaat."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alarm"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alarm"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "AlarmMessage" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A per-alarm message node — the hub for this occurrence's independent facets: mda:concernsPatient (the shared, persistent patient — the merge anchor operational inference reasons across alarms over) and mda:triggeredBy (the device whose technical structure this alarm implicates), reached as siblings rather than one gatewaying the other."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Een per-alarm berichtknooppunt — het knooppunt voor de onafhankelijke facetten van deze gebeurtenis: mda:concernsPatient en mda:triggeredBy, als nevengeschikte eigenschappen bereikt."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alarm Message"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmMessage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alarmbericht"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Alarm> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "AlarmType" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A generic, archetypal alarm definition independent of any specific device instance or patient encounter. Captures the default device, sensor, and signal structure associated with a class of alarm."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Een generieke, archetypische alarmdefinitie, onafhankelijk van een specifieke apparaatinstantie of patiëntencounter. Legt de standaard apparaat-, sensor- en signaalstructuur vast die samenhangt met een klasse van alarmen."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alarm Type"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AlarmType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alarmtype"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "AnatomicalPosition" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De anatomische positie van een sensor op het lichaam."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The anatomical position of a sensor on the body."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Anatomical Position"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#AnatomicalPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Anatomische Positie"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Individuated> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "Component" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A physical or functional part of a medical device (e.g. a connection port, power unit, or heating element). mda:Sensor is the specialisation that additionally produces a measurable signal — every sensor is a component, but not every component senses."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Een fysiek of functioneel onderdeel van een medisch apparaat (bijv. een aansluitpoort, voedingseenheid of verwarmingselement). mda:Sensor is de specialisatie die daarnaast een meetbaar signaal produceert — elke sensor is een onderdeel, maar niet elk onderdeel meet."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Component"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Onderdeel"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "CriticalComponent" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De subklasse van mda:Component waarvan het loskoppelen betekent dat het apparaat zelf niet beschikbaar is (bijv. de datapoort, de stroomaansluiting) — in tegenstelling tot een randonderdeel waarvan het loskoppelen slechts een subsysteemwaarschuwing is (bijv. een matrasverwarming)."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The subclass of mda:Component whose own disconnection means the device itself is unavailable (e.g. the data-link port, the power inlet) — as opposed to a peripheral component whose disconnection is only a subsystem-level warning (e.g. a mattress heater). This class exists so the propagation rule using it can be precise: unconditionally true for CriticalComponent, never assumed for mda:Component as a whole — see mda:hasOperationState's comment below on why mda:hasComponent was deliberately dropped from its propertyChainAxiom. The rule itself, and which concrete vocabulary-level component types (e.g. component:ConnectionUnit, component:PowerUnit) are tagged as members of this class, both live in 2_READOUT/outcome/inference.ttl's Component operational-state propagation section — the rule's hasValue target (a specific operation-state concept) is catalogue vocabulary, so it cannot be asserted here, but this class it's written over is a plain structural distinction with no vocabulary dependency, so it belongs in this TBox, not duplicated per component type down there."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Critical component"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#CriticalComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Kritiek onderdeel"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Individuated> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "Device" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medical device that generates alarms."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Een medisch apparaat dat alarmen genereert."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Apparaat"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Device> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device"@en .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Component> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Sensor> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#nodeKind> <http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Individuated> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "FunctionalUnit" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De module van een apparaat die de berekeningslogica voor een bepaalde meetmogelijkheid huisvest (bijv. een ECG-module, een SpO2-module) — in de volksmond vaak 'de sensor' genoemd, maar hier onderscheiden van mda:Sensor, dat enkel de fysieke probe is. Een functionele eenheid leest van één of meer sensoren en zet, via één of meer mda:SignalAnalysis-stappen, hun signalen om in metrieken. Een specialisatie van mda:Component. Disjunct verklaard met mda:Sensor vanwege precies die volkstaal-verwarring."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The module of a device that houses the computation logic for a particular measurement capability (e.g. an ECG module, an SpO2 module) — often called 'the sensor' colloquially, but distinct here from mda:Sensor, which is only the physical probe. A functional unit reads from one or more sensors and, via one or more mda:SignalAnalysis steps, turns their signals into metrics. A specialisation of mda:Component. Declared disjoint with mda:Sensor precisely because of that colloquial conflation — the two are easy to confuse in exactly the way this class's own name tries to prevent, so a node accidentally typed as both is now an inconsistency a reasoner catches rather than a silent modelling error."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Functional unit"@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Functionele eenheid"@nl .
# 
# http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "Laterality" .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "De lateraliteit (links, rechts, bilateraal) van een sensorpositie."@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The laterality (left, right, bilateral) of a sensor position."@en .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lateraliteit"@nl .
<http://example.org/model-device-alarm-knowledge#Laterality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Laterality"@en .
